  "body": "Concurrent first visits from multiple tabs can return HTTP500 on the unique navigation-preference constraint. Also, the published web payload (`favorite`, `pinned`, `pinOrder`) is rejected with HTTP400 because the strict decoder expects internal `npu` field names. This change fixes UX-260917-031 and UX-260917-034 with an atomic unique-key upsert and strict canonical decoding that retains the legacy payload. Mixed schemas, unknown fields and caller-supplied account IDs remain rejected. No migration is added.\n\nVerification: the old binary deterministically failed the controlled 16-request HTTP/PostgreSQL race. The prior corrected build passed concurrent visits/counts and exposed the separate settings-decoder failure; that failed gate is not counted as success. Current head9213 adds generated canonical/legacy round trips and real HTTP settings, isolation, denial and revocation cases. Its hosted backend gate is still running; applicable completed checks and the exact-head independent approval are green. TLC verified 16 distinct states under the stated finite/fair database assumptions, and the legacy negative control produced the expected counterexample. The model covers state transitions, not wire decoding or usability.\n\nMerge normally after the corrected runtime gate and review threads pass. Recheck current main/provider integration and release ownership before the guarded immutable-image/snapshot/lease/canary rollout. The earlier #431 backend release is complete at2f01; this PR has made no production mutation.\n",
